  "summary": "Off-registry git dependency executed at install time",
  "details": "package.json declares its sole dependency as a git URL pinned to a commit SHA on github.com/agustedone/test-supply-npm-git-prepare-proof-4 rather than a registry version range. On npm install, npm fetches this source and runs any lifecycle scripts (the name implies a `prepare` hook) from whatever the repository returns. The shipped index.js is a stub, so the manifest line is the entire installable surface — code execution on the installer's machine is controlled by whoever controls that GitHub repository, outside the registry's integrity checks.",
